prevents Kyiv from intercepting Russian attacks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Czechia: Scores protest against public media reform</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f90bf22b12c6627967f8f491efd9d319f39dbc00dc13b2aaf9509ff18e22403e</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:07:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T19:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czechia-scores-protest-against-public-media-reform/a-79953057--804bd6cc316f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czechia-scores-protest-against-public-media-reform/a-79953057?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of people gathered to protest against the government's plan to abolish broadcasting fees. Critics say the nationalist coalition would like to secure control over the media.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Estonia closes border to Russia after suspected drone factory arson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26d4bf44bbbbd4787c95ed2dd22b2ed9bd9ea1537250d7bddc22588305296b63</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T18:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/estonia-closes-border-to-russia-after-suspected-drone-factory-arson/a-79953115--0e59b4bde9de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/estonia-closes-border-to-russia-after-suspected-drone-factory-arson/a-79953115?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Estonia has accused Russia of conducting hybrid warfare after a drone factory was set alight in Viimsi. Now it will close its border crossings at the start of December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nearly 1,600 migrants arrive on Spain's Canary Islands in one day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e699fb563c26a99c46aac05f89b6f1bd7d3c1a42aa56982c26eab98c73ec9bf</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T18:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nearly-1-600-migrants-arrive-on-spain-s-canary-islands-in-one-day/a-79952941--709bffa2c1cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nearly-1-600-migrants-arrive-on-spain-s-canary-islands-in-one-day/a-79952941?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The majority of the migrants who arrived on the islands on Saturday came from Senegal, Gambia, and Guinea. The surge in arrivals to the Canaries comes after Spain's Ceuta recently faced a migration crisis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cape Verde goes to the polls in presidential vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:481a3cf15ba0efdc27d3d59f86792bce1d4737060748b0c05c1a5711bcbb35fb</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cape-verde-goes-to-the-polls-in-presidential-vote/a-79952606--0f20123309fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cape-verde-goes-to-the-polls-in-presidential-vote/a-79952606?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Known for its political stability and good governance, the island nation will vote for its next president. About 420,000 people are eligible to vote</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German economy returns to growth, so why is the country still worried?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06803c304e203065cb383c5eb7f1c33c67cd8de7143a31702578866c91818d70</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220--24d2aa1d0aab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German economy is growing again, albeit slightly. However, economists warn that without reforms, higher productivity and solid public finances, a loss of prosperity and growing debt threaten future generations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo heads to high Andes on final leg of South America tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:883b458642404677edfea46a62a5e4b411cd0319998ef125e94486821ba88dcb</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-heads-to-high-andes-on-final-leg-of-south-america-tour/a-79952884--2d76c56d2268.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-heads-to-high-andes-on-final-leg-of-south-america-tour/a-79952884?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leo, originally from Chicago, served as the bishop of Chiclayo from 2015 until 2023. He is expected to spotlight Indigenous rights and environmental protection on the final leg of his tour.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Despite restrictive abortion laws, Poland's 'Abortomat' — a locker that dispenses abortion pills — helps women who want to end a pregnancy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3522b983202a91710c057024bb40ff8bdc3930b2b48d00d99c7f82fd606e93fe</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/polish-activists-face-opposition-as-they-make-abortion-more-accessible/a-79943914--39db4083c558.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/despite-restrictive-abortion-laws-poland-s-abortomat-a-locker-that-dispenses-abortion-pills-helps-women-who-want-to-end-a-pregnancy/a-79943914?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Abortion laws in Poland are very restrictive. Activists there have found a new way to help women wanting to terminate a pregnancy: the "Abortomat," a locker that dispenses abortion pills. But they face fierce opposition.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>ASEAN offers Myanmar's sidelined leaders a path back to summits, but says restrictions will stay until there is meaningful progress on its peace plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eea1da43e56b2a9597cb57af5fda0d94f483457362e4b5f5fd6771b563461ad0</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/asean-offers-myanmar-s-sidelined-leaders-a-path-back-to-summits-but-says-restrictions-will-stay-unti/a-79951878--8a50f9fda2bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/asean-offers-myanmar-s-sidelined-leaders-a-path-back-to-summits-but-says-restrictions-will-stay-until-there-is-meaningful-progress-on-its-peace-plan/a-79951878?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Southeast Asian leaders have agreed to engage Myanmar in stages after years of excluding its leaders from high-level meetings. The bloc says Myanmar could regain full representation if it makes progress on a peace plan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Macron urges unity as Francophonie summit opens in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f0e94504940f216110a2d3a808bf22f4d4d0256f637c162e19717f034d3675c</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-urges-unity-as-francophonie-summit-opens-in-cambodia/a-79951201--02576530ba13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-urges-unity-as-francophonie-summit-opens-in-cambodia/a-79951201?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leaders of French-speaking nations gathered in Phnom Penh as a row over who should lead the Francophonie and Congo’s threat to quit put pressure on Macron to broker consensus.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Germany holds national day of remembrance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63a1a1fd57a847889b3c6680d5b668768d8850e70a26d4ac988e216a90eec1ab</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-holds-national-day-of-remembrance/live-79947500--7252f2ee958f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-holds-national-day-of-remembrance/live-79947500?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Events are being held for 'Volkstrauertag,' a day commemorating victims of war and oppression. Meanwhile, experts say the country is headed for a budget crisis. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How AI is likely to change Germany's job market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:424164d16dce443a12adcf750f9a219bdd0a5796562222bf2da16bca1eb493b1</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T05:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597--3a5b2bd9406d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The scale of the economic disruption caused by AI has led even conservative politicians to talk about universal basic income. But economists aren't convinced, and campaigners think we need to ask deeper questions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands continue to protest across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fbd5952158bb213e2f54eddae1db26adc5b7d7cc36b0b20e15de88defe79d6f</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T00:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tens-of-thousands-continue-to-protest-across-france/a-79950503--f335770faa0d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tens-of-thousands-continue-to-protest-across-france/a-79950503?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some 106,000 people marched through French cities for a fifth consecutive weekend of protests, marking the lowest turnout in recent weeks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines wins first Eurovision Song Contest Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d435ffde3ac84f2046a0b1f85642ada38ad2443a92fb9e363d66df88e2635bdb</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T22:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-wins-first-eurovision-song-contest-asia/a-79950050--13c562f8bc59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-wins-first-eurovision-song-contest-asia/a-79950050?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Eleven countries took part in the competition in Bangkok. Teenage winner Carmelle Collado's winning dance song is a tribute to Filipino women.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX completes first-ever spaceship capture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82ced7fdc0c37f048360c41609fcd98e4ad1b42872e21e2952b8e15a62613a36</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:08:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spacex-completes-first-ever-spaceship-capture/a-79950275--9c34840ad14b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spacex-completes-first-ever-spaceship-capture/a-79950275?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The successful recovery of SpaceX's Starship marks a breakthrough in founder Elon Musk's goal of developing a fully reusable rocket system.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's 2027 budget: A record €561 billion and a mountain of debt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:042f5b5730245cdf1895b319463c9738c9b8341ea8a62fb46b616434bd9d6b6c</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-_561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216--747b01c10ad0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-€561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2027 federal budget proposal has finally been hammered out and is set for a vote in parliament. What are the government's policy priorities in defense, infrastructure, the economy and social spending?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73e115da96d191261040ede358e24d0ac0a2822b7f378ed5b8ac5c2e88fdf873</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Sudan pushes back elections amid violent flare-ups</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:877c10bf318f969dd1798441c9f7398bcb68b3ff4eb9de6803e5dc0fff1e8e68</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-pushes-back-elections-amid-violent-flare-ups/a-79949622--9cf2f881ff78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-pushes-back-elections-amid-violent-flare-ups/a-79949622?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Sudan has been independent from Sudan since 2011, and has not yet held national elections. Since then, the country faces cycles of violence after a civil war led to a tenuous peace deal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: Duffy says 'incompetence' or bad tech to blame for flight haltings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b63b1249fc3905fe152a43f48358c01f73b59233b5329376b1602c7282f45b43</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-duffy-says-incompetence-or-bad-tech-to-blame-for-flight-haltings/a-79949977--1dd9eb14fa53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-duffy-says-incompetence-or-bad-tech-to-blame-for-flight-haltings/a-79949977?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Air carriers in the US canceled some 16,000 flights over the past 24 hours in the biggest such grounding since 9/11. Officials hinted that incompetence or faulty equipment, not malfeasance, is the cause.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: 'Iranian' content farms reach millions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9e36a8d14ce76e4346af4966de2ee0a25d3f63c693103ac55e6dce94d0849e0</id><updated>2026-11-15T21:06:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-iranian-content-farms-reach-millions/a-79934190--0e43f1d33817.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-iranian-content-farms-reach-millions/a-79934190?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several social media accounts claiming to represent the Iranian military show signs of being part of so-called content farms. DW Fact Check looks at how they operate and how users can spot them.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
